  "articleBody": "It's a common scenario: you're excited about new crown molding, but your walls or ceilings aren't perfectly straight. Don't worry, it's a very normal challenge in older homes, and even some newer ones! The key is understanding that precision is paramount with crown molding because any gaps or misalignments can be pretty noticeable. We always start by carefully measuring the actual corner angles in your room, which often aren't a perfect 90 degrees. This helps us make cuts that truly fit your unique space. Sometimes, we'll even use a reference line to guide the installation, ensuring everything stays consistent despite minor imperfections. We also make sure to fasten the molding directly into studs or the top plate, not just the drywall, for a secure fit that can help bridge small gaps. When walls are especially uneven, a professional touch can really make a difference, as we have techniques for coping joints and carefully filling tiny discrepancies to make everything look seamless. Don't let imperfect walls stop you from achieving that finished look; a little expert finesse goes a long way. If you're tackling a room with tricky angles or uneven surfaces, give HH Remodeling LLC a call for a flawless finish in the greater Denver area.",
